Q3. What is a Docker Storage Driver?

Interview Ready Answer

A Docker Storage Driver is the component responsible for managing Docker
image layers and the container's writable layer. It implements Docker's
layered filesystem and allows multiple images to share common layers
efficiently.

Definition

Storage Driver
- Manages image layers.
- Manages writable layer.
- Implements layered filesystem.

Purpose

• Manage image layers.
• Manage container writable layer.
• Improve storage efficiency.
• Enable layer sharing.

Note

Common storage drivers include:
- overlay2 (Most commonly used)
- aufs
- btrfs
- zfs

(Only overlay2 is worth remembering for campus interviews.)

======================================================================

Q4. How do you create a Docker Volume?

Interview Ready Answer

A Docker Volume is created using the following command:

docker volume create <volume_name>

The volume can then be mounted to one or more containers to provide
persistent storage.

Purpose

• Create persistent storage.
• Store application data.
• Store database files.

======================================================================

Q5. Which command lists all Docker Volumes?

Interview Ready Answer

The following command lists all Docker Volumes available on the local
Docker host:

docker volume ls

Purpose

• View existing volumes.
• Verify created volumes.
• Manage Docker storage.

